WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.111
This lesson becomes clearer when before the worked example, separate node current balance from loop voltage balance instead of trying to do all the circuit reasoning at once.

2
00:00:07.111 --> 00:00:14.222
Rule 1 means junction current balance: Current conservation belongs at a node where routes split or recombine.

3
00:00:14.222 --> 00:00:21.333
Rule 2 means loop voltage balance: Voltage rises and drops balance around a complete closed path.

4
00:00:21.333 --> 00:00:28.444
Main trap means mixing the rules: A circuit question feels harder than it is when the node rule and the loop rule are blended together.

5
